# Originals live in R2, not git. Keeping them out is what stops the
# repo ballooning — git stores every version of a binary forever, so a
# single accidental commit of media/ can't really be undone.
media/
Incoming Exports/
Portfolio.bsdesign
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# NOTE: this file used to list itself, which left it untracked and
# living only on the Mac. That worked right up until it didn't — a
# fresh clone would have had no ignore rules at all, so the next
# `deploy-dev` would `git add -A` the whole media/ folder into history.
# Tracking it means the rules travel with the repo.